# Verify — etude-rep: worktree leak tests scan the shared TMPDIR

## Track

Fast-lane (test-only, localized, unambiguous): lightweight plan → do → verify →
ONE gate on the verified diff. Not fast-lane-able surfaces (money, security,
data-egress, schema migration) are not touched — this changes two test functions
and adds one test helper. No production code changes: `git diff` on
`internal/worktree/worktree.go` is empty.

## Plan (recorded here; no separate plan gate on the fast lane)

`snapshotWorktreeTempDirs` scans the process-global `os.TempDir()` for entries
named `etude-worktree-*`. `worktree.Checkout` is also called from the `liverun`,
`bench` and `cli` test packages, which `go test ./...` runs as separate
concurrent test binaries against the SAME `TMPDIR`. A dir another package created
between the before- and after-snapshot is therefore attributed to the `Checkout`
under test.

Fix: point `os.TempDir()` at a per-test directory for the duration of each leak
test (`t.Setenv("TMPDIR", t.TempDir())`), so the scan can only ever see dirs this
test's own `Checkout` created. Nothing about what the assertion checks changes —
only which directory it looks in. Rejected alternative: filtering the snapshot by
mtime or pid, which is heuristic and would still race.

## Diff

```diff
+// isolateTempDir points os.TempDir() at a per-test directory for the rest of the
+// test. [full rationale comment in the diff]
+func isolateTempDir(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Helper()
+	t.Setenv("TMPDIR", t.TempDir())
+}
```

plus one `isolateTempDir(t)` call as the first statement of
`TestNoTempDirLeakOnSHANotFound` and `TestNoTempDirLeakOnWorktreeAddFailure`.

Neither test calls `t.Parallel()`, so `t.Setenv` is legal in both.

## Evidence

**Failure reproduced on clean `origin/main` (b38cece), before the fix:**

```
--- FAIL: TestNoTempDirLeakOnWorktreeAddFailure (0.13s)
    worktree_test.go:441: Checkout leaked temp dir(s) on worktree-add failure: [etude-worktree-3677800337]
FAIL	github.com/joshuavial/etude/internal/worktree	8.643s
make: *** [test] Error 1
```

The same test passed in isolation (`go test ./internal/worktree/ -run
TestNoTempDirLeakOnWorktreeAddFailure`), which is the signature of cross-package
interference rather than a defect in `Checkout`.

**Root cause confirmed by inspection, not inferred:**
`internal/worktree/worktree.go:57` is the only `MkdirTemp(\"\", \"etude-worktree-*\")`
call site; `worktree.Checkout` callers outside the package are
`internal/liverun/engine.go:229`, `:315`, `internal/liverun/replay_forward.go:54`,
`internal/bench/run.go:135`, `internal/cli/replay.go:191`.

**NEGATIVE CONTROL — the guard is load-bearing, not merely green.**
With the fix applied, `os.RemoveAll(dir)` was deleted from the `addErr != nil`
branch of `Checkout` and the tests re-run:

```
--- PASS: TestNoTempDirLeakOnSHANotFound (0.08s)
    worktree_test.go:456: Checkout leaked temp dir(s) on worktree-add failure: [etude-worktree-1240529042]
--- FAIL: TestNoTempDirLeakOnWorktreeAddFailure (0.09s)
```

The test still catches a real leak. `worktree.go` was then restored; `git diff`
on it is empty, confirmed before staging.

**Full parallel suite, twice, both exit 0:**

```
=== run 1 ===  go test ./...  exit=0
=== run 2 ===  go test ./...  exit=0
```

`make test` and `make lint` both green.

